"""pt-BR batch 4 — contact, help, terms, privacy.

Terms and privacy render the pg.legal_language notice whenever the page is not
in English, so the Portuguese is explicitly a convenience translation and the
English governs. That matters more here than for Danish: Brazil has its own
data-protection law (LGPD) and this policy is written against the GDPR, so a
Portuguese text that reads as authoritative could imply commitments the English
does not make.
"""
